Package: jmp2r
Type: Package
Title: Read JMP Data Tables Without JMP
Version: 0.2.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("jmp2r contributors", role = "aut"),
    person("eisuke-inoue386", role = "cre",
           email = "262287482+eisuke-inoue386@users.noreply.github.com"),
    person("David", "Mathers", role = c("ctb", "cph")),
    person("Jaakko", "Ruohio", role = c("ctb", "cph")))
Description: Reads supported binary JMP data tables using base R, without
    requiring JMP, Python, Julia, or a compiler. Preserves decoded column
    metadata and original source bytes, and reports information that could
    not be interpreted. Also reads a deliberately restricted literal subset
    of embedded-data JRP scripts without executing code. External references
    and dynamic scripts are rejected. The undocumented binary reader is
    derived from the MIT-licensed JMPReader.jl and jmp-convert projects.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports: utils
NeedsCompilation: no
URL: https://github.com/eisuke-inoue386/jmp2r
BugReports: https://github.com/eisuke-inoue386/jmp2r/issues
